        "login": ""
      },
      "authorAssociation": "NONE",
      "body": "If this change is made, I would say that that advice should be quite specific - in addition to base64 as mentioned, you could also see session tokens in other reversible forms, such as encrypted tokens. \r\n\r\nAssuming adequate entropy, a hashed session token would effectively be impossible to reserve - if it was encrypted, you suddenly have another encryption key in play, that if exposed in a config file or the like, could render the protection of the token moot. ",
